A||||10||HAGS||Problems with TBI||||1||
Z||000000||HAGS||12-22-2000||12:00 AM||||Ok, yesterday my air filter cover ripped off one of the rods it screws onto....it ripped in the worst spot possible, down in the TBI, anyone know if I can replace it, and any ideas on how im gonna get it out with nothing to grab onto?  I'll go out now and take some pictures to get an idea...it also started smoking from the TBI after the rod broke, and was getting knocking today.<P>In other news, I've replaced all the mounts, the engine still hits the trunk.<P>My tachometer doesnt work.<P>86' 2m4||||reg||1
Z||000001||HAGS||12-22-2000||12:59 AM||||ok, I got the pictures on my site but havent sized them yet, they are about 570k each in size so I'll just post the links<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/camppen/filterlid.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/camppen/filterlid.jpg</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/camppen/tbi.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/camppen/tbi.jpg</A> <P>Just noticed something while im waiting for them to upload...looks like there was an explosion in the bore, its black and charred around the edges...I clean that thing alot, I'll go check to see if its just some shadow...||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-22-2000||10:58 AM||||I'm not sure off top of my head just how the air cleaner attachment is handled on the 300 TBI. I can't look it up right now. It can be fixed but it may not be very easy. If you have to take the TBI apart just get the rebuild kit for it and do that while it's off.<P>The threads can probably be fixed with a Helicoil IF there is enough metal to alow an over sized hole to be drilled to accept the coil.<P>If the threads are damaged it might be easier to locate a used TBI in a scrap yard. I don't know what that would cost. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bob Englert||12-22-2000||12:43 PM||||It seems to me that it might be easier to just replace the TBI with a junkyard unit.  84's are pretty common in the yards, so hopefully you won't have trouble finding one.<P>Did you change the the dogbone when you changed the mounts?  Did you replace all 3 mounts (1 motor and 2 trans)?  If you have a 4 sp you might consider putting poly bushings in your dogbone.  It really tightened up the motor in my 85 4 cyl.  There is a lot of vibration when it is used in an auto car when idling in gear, but it isn't too bad with a manual trans, except when the A/C is on.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000004||Xtreme Fiero's||12-22-2000||10:31 PM||||ah... Running lean W/ to much spark advance......Memories..........<P>I miss my headache  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Does the car still run well? you probably damaged the MAP sensor and some other junk Save money down the road and just get a Holley TBI<P>did/do you have any engine codes?<P>You do have me beat in the "Beating the crap out of the TBI" area  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||HAGS||12-22-2000||10:42 PM||||I replaced all 3 mounts, im about ready to go poly, right now I have the whole TBI unit out for cleaning although it wasnt too bad, even on the bottom, other than not being able to give it any gas it also knocks now like a diesal truck.<BR>Before the problems I used 89 or 93 octane when available.  I doubt a new TBI will fix the knocking as I've heard in other threads that its probably bent rod or something... I've heard the knocking once before, my car died at a stop light and my dad came to give me a jump start, for about a mile on the drive home it was knocking but quit, that was over a month ago and I've driven it about 1000 miles since then with no sign of the knocking...then im going to the post office and im approaching a truck and I hear the knocking, at first I think its him but it only gets louder as Im breaking away from him at 90 mph.<P>I have an 86.5 2m4 Automatic<P>What would I see if I were to take the black cover off the top of the engine? Is it safe for an 18 year old beginner to do in his driveway and be able to put back on after getting a quick view?  Does anyone have pictures of what I would see??||||reg||1
Z||000006||HAGS||12-22-2000||10:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Xtreme Fiero's:<BR><B><BR>did/do you have any engine codes?<P>You do have me beat in the "Beating the crap out of the TBI" area   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I get occasional check engine lights but I've seen no pattern in how they come, I'll be driving at 90-100 mph and it comes on for 10 seconds then goes out...or at 45 mph...it comes and goes as it pleases with no engine response as it happens.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bob Englert||12-23-2000||08:50 AM||||If the check engine light comes on then you need to read the codes to see what the ECM is telling you.  Get a Haynes manual to see the codes and how to check them.<P>Driving a 4 cyl Fiero with the problems you describe at 90-100 mph sounds light abuse to me!  Take it easy until you get things fixed, please.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||12-23-2000||12:11 PM||||I looked at the haynes fiero book. I can't find by EFI book. It looks like you should be able to extract the peice of the broken air cleaner stud from the TBI. I can't tell how big a job that is w/o my EFI book or a 300 TBI to look at.||||reg||1
Z||000009||HAGS||12-23-2000||06:00 PM||||Well I took all the push rods out, none are bent and appear to be in good condition...so the knocking is from somewhere else...where could it be??  <P>And for the TBI, to take that part out would be way too much work then I would have to put another one in, im just gonna goto a junkyard and see if I can get a replacement, or if I get a job I'll get the holley||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||12-23-2000||08:29 PM||||you should be able to find that TBI in a bunch of GM cars. <P>You may have to swap the IAC. There are 2 styles of IAC. The connectors are diferant but I think the rest is the same. (Chop off the IAC connector from the donor car just in case. Leave as much wire on it as you can.)||||reg||1
